When the carrier drafts its Master B/L, a card opens under the instructions. It shows the critical information first:
• where it stands: drafted, approved, issued, surrendered for delivery;
• anything that differs from what you sent, at the top, your value next to the carrier's;
• six key facts, each marked ✓ (same as sent) or ≠ (changed): the document and originals, the vessel and voyage, the shipper, the consignee, the ports, and the containers with their weight and seals.
Show all fields opens the field-by-field comparison. Click the card's title to fold it away. If the draft is right, Approve draft. If something needs correcting, fix the shipment and use Send update. A task sits on the export office's Kanban until the draft is approved. When the carrier issues it, the shipment takes the Master B/L number and B/L Issued completes. When the B/L is surrendered for delivery, the carrier marks the instructions complete.
A House B/L you have issued travels inside the Master's instructions where the destination's advance filing needs House-level data (EU ICS2, US AMS, Mercosur). Its packages then need their package code, and its HS code the destination tariff's digits; the submit tells you if either is missing.
